{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Use Spring XD's existing module configuration mechanism for Rabbit sink batching properties (batchingEnabled, batchingSize).",
    "For Gradle build option, leverage Spring Boot's MODULE layout feature (assuming issue #2187 is resolved or a workaround is feasible).",
    "Acceptance tests for hdfs-dataset will be written using Spring XD's acceptance test framework (likely based on Cucumber/JUnit).",
    "Compression extension will introduce a CompressionCodec interface and allow configuration via Spring's resource loader.",
    "Performance benchmarks will use the existing benchmark suite (assumed to be JMH or similar) with modified configurations.",
    "DIRT runtime DB disable will be implemented via a conditional @Configuration class that only initializes DB beans when enabled.",
    "RxJava processor module will implement the existing Processor interface (or a new ReactiveProcessor interface) and be built as a separate module."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The developer has full access to the Spring XD codebase and necessary infrastructure (RabbitMQ, HDFS, etc.) for testing.",
    "The Spring Boot issue #2187 is resolved in the version we are using, or a workaround is feasible within the estimated effort.",
    "The benchmark environment is already set up and can be run with different configurations without major setup time.",
    "The core interface contract for processor modules is already defined and stable.",
    "All changes are backward compatible and do not require major refactoring of existing modules.",
    "The team follows standard Spring development practices (unit tests, integration tests, documentation).",
    "Effort estimates include time for code writing, testing, and documentation but not for external dependencies (e.g., waiting for CI builds)."
  ],
